docs/seo/gsc-404-2026-09.csv is the Search Console "Not found (404)" export
(326 URLs, report dated 2026-09-03). build-redirects now reads it instead of
the seed list.

Matcher improvements so the full export doesn't collapse into 164 × 410:

- Redirect stubs (Astro meta-refresh pages in dist/) are indexed with their
  destination and resolved, so a rule never 301s onto a stub (no 301→stub→301
  chains, e.g. /en/collection/puerto-rico/... now lands on the real EN page).
  A stub pointing at a missing page (unpublished polymer continent hubs)
  falls through to hub matching instead of being reported as "exists".
- docs/seo/manual-overrides.json: 56 hand-reviewed pairs — the 32 legacy
  /en/glossary/<english-slug>/ terms mapped to their v2 /en/glossary/ slugs,
  plus MPC, State Bank New Brunswick, City Bank New Haven, Giori, Rency,
  Santa Marta ¼ real, Malaysia polymer, Philippines Victory series, blog and
  editorial paths. Targets are validated as live, non-stub v2 pages at build.
- category-map.json: v1 sections that vanished in v2 (certificados-de-pago-
  militar, emisiones-promocionales, moneda-colonial, moneda-colonial-espanola,
  reserva-federal, pop-art, mozambique/nigeria/papua-nueva-guinea, and their
  EN counterparts) → their v2 hubs.
- New `legacy-dc` rule: pre-v1 Dreamweaver root files (/billete-colombia-*.dc,
  /catalogo-*.dc.html, …) → section hub by prefix.
- New `glossary-hub` rule for unmatched glossary terms.

Result for 476 rows: 195 existing, 56 manual, 51 legacy-dc, 27 category-hub,
117 hub-fallback (low confidence, listed for review), 7 last-slug,
2 last-slug-hreflang, 3 fuzzy, 2 exists, 16 gone (410: dated WordPress posts,
{{ item.url }} template junk, one truncated URL).

verify-redirects treats stubs as non-live; the worker test picks a 410 from
the current map instead of a fixed seed URL. Tests: 176 pass. Wrangler
dry-run bundles the 160K lookup JSON fine.

